# --- ADR-0067 phase 4: the second committed skill root is now a generated VIEW ------------
# `.agents/skills` is STILL a runtime skill root — both Claude and Codex load it, and it is half of
# the union `<FsggKitSkillRoots>` + `<FsggKitViewSkillRoots>` declares in
# `.config/kit/FS.GG.Kit.receiver.proj`. It is simply no longer a second COMMITTED copy of
# `.claude/skills`: `scripts/skill-view generate` resolves it at checkout (FS-GG/.github#1676, #1748).
#
# It is git-ignored rather than committed because a COMMITTED symlink does not degrade safely: under
# `git -c core.symlinks=false` (the git-for-Windows default without Developer Mode) it checks out as a
# small regular text file, and both runtimes then exit 0 with zero skills and no diagnostic
# (ADR-0067 §6). An untracked generated root fails loudly instead — `scripts/skill-view check`, with
# both its declaration and resolution lanes, runs on the required `skill-view-check` context.
#
# Do NOT commit this root, and do NOT delete this line to "fix" a missing directory. Regenerate it:
#   bash scripts/skill-view generate --source .claude/skills --roots ".agents/skills"
/.agents/skills
